The edit lock must not outlive the editor — 12 Sept.

Nicholas Coffin's lock sat in the file from 17:40 to 20:10 on 11 Sept because he closed the
tab rather than pressing Done, so exitEdit() never ran. It never kept anyone OUT — the Edit
gate has always honoured LOCK_MS, six minutes — but the record stayed, so the board's own
data claimed an editor who had gone home.

  · lockLive(l) — one place decides whether a lock is live; the Edit gate asks it rather
    than repeating the arithmetic.
  · tidyDeadLock() — clears an expired lock, in memory only, on load and on the sync poll.
    A viewer must never write to the shared file, so the next editor persists the tidy-up.
  · pagehide — closing the tab hands the lock back, best effort, on top of the expiry rather
    than instead of it. pagehide not beforeunload, which is unreliable on iOS.

Tests: render 303 passed / 1 failed (pre-existing on untouched HEAD, unrelated) ·
